1
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:21,960
Tips for inspiring creativity.

2
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,160
Listening to different sounds

3
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:26,220
to stimulate auditory imagination.

4
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:28,900
Listen,

5
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:32,619
the bird songs of different pitches.

6
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:34,920
They seem to form different scales.

7
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,640
You can collect them

8
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:39,640
as material for percussion.

9
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:45,690
And the rustling of fallen leaves.

10
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:52,160
The sounds of people exercising.

11
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:58,960
And the sound of the wind.

12
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:03,320
I found inspiration for the chorus.

13
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:13,760
Actually, when I write songs,

14
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:14,920
a lot of my inspiration

15
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:17,000
comes from my own memories.

16
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:20,560
For example,

17
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:22,560
the song 'Wish'.

18
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:26,160
Which girl did you write this song for?

19
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:27,720
It's a guy.

20
00:01:30,039 --> 00:01:31,840
I wrote it for a roommate of mine.

21
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,920
He was my best friend in college.

22
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:35,759
We agreed that

23
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:38,120
we would make music together after graduation

24
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:39,640
and form the best band.

25
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:44,360
We used to come here often to talk about creation,

26
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:45,420
find inspiration,

27
00:01:45,759 --> 00:01:47,220
and talk about our dreams.

28
00:01:49,039 --> 00:01:50,200
But then one day,

29
00:01:50,479 --> 00:01:51,720
he suddenly told me

30
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:55,100
he was going to give up.

31
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,560
He said

32
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,759
making music has too many uncertainties,

33
00:01:59,759 --> 00:02:02,560
and it would be better to find a job in his hometown.

34
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:05,320
I didn't expect that after graduation,

35
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,650
he would actually go back to his hometown.

36
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,840
So we lost touch after that.

37
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,760
Every time I come here

38
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,600
and hum that song,

39
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:17,920
I think of him.

40
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:40,480
I think when Ning Caichen and Nie Xiaoqian

41
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:41,840
met for the first time,

42
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,650
his feelings were probably

43
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:46,720
the same as mine when I first met you.

44
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:48,720
So,

45
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:52,160
how did you feel when you first met me?

46
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,280
Nervous.

47
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:56,840
Nervous?

48
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,840
When Ning Caichen first met Nie Xiaoqian,

49
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,760
with no experience at all,

50
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:04,360
he might have been just like me,

51
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,620
his mind full of panic,

52
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:08,140
only thinking he wasn't good enough.

53
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:12,010
Ning Caichen thought Nie Xiaoqian was so beautiful,

54
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:14,000
while he was just a poor scholar.

55
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:18,020
Nie Xiaoqian probably thought Ning Caichen was a good man too.

56
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:19,320
But

57
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:22,220
she was just a harmful wild ghost.

58
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:23,280
So

59
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:26,200
when they first met,

60
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:29,340
all they thought about were their own flaws.

61
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:32,980
So the first feeling after falling for someone.

62
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:36,140
It's an inferiority complex.

63
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:37,920
It's shrinking back.

64
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,880
I can't believe you're a director.

65
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:39,120
I even went looking for you at Zeri Bar the next day.

66
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:41,520
Why can't I understand what you're saying?

67
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,200
You know,

68
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,480
I signed with the company when I was 18.

69
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:58,010
After signing, I started running schedules,

70
00:04:58,159 --> 00:04:58,920
making records,

71
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,250
and I was busy non-stop.

72
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:02,290
You asked about my dating history.

73
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:03,960
What could I say?

74
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:09,880
Ning Jin.

75
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:11,560
Let me ask you.

76
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:14,770
Do you have feelings for me?

77
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:16,120
Yes.

78
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:12,080
So,

79
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:14,160
the methods I taught you to find inspiration,

80
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:15,240
did they help you?

81
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,410
They were very helpful.

82
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:18,400
That's good.

83
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:26,360
I...

84
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:28,760
I can stay further away from you.

85
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:31,010
Keep a one-meter distance.

86
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:32,120
Three meters.

87
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:34,080
Or five meters.

88
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:34,480
You...

89
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:35,560
Jin Xi.

90
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:39,040
Come here.

91
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,580
I dodged you this time.

92
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,760
You're good.

93
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:05,560
Wanna try again?

94
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:07,560
I-I didn't mean that.

95
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:08,080
I mean,

96
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,560
because I didn't know if you wanted to kiss me

97
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,560
or not.

98
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,920
Because the last time I kissed you,

99
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:13,960
you pushed me away.

100
00:07:13,960 --> 00:07:15,440
And when you kissed me,

101
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,360
I didn't push you away.

102
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:16,760
So,

103
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:19,280
didn't you say to keep work and private life separate?

104
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:20,160
I was thinking,

105
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:22,040
maybe after the performance is over,

106
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,560
we could continue our relationship.

107
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,000
I...

108
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,080
Jin Xi, I like you.

109
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:30,160
I don't want to wait anymore.

110
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:31,560
If

111
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:34,040
I kiss you now,

112
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,000
would you still hide?

113
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:10,840
I'm glad you're here to listen to me about this.

114
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:13,920
Otherwise, you don't know how hard it is for me to hold it in.

115
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:15,440
My best friend

116
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:17,640
is dating a superstar.

117
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:21,840
It's literally a plot from a TV drama.

118
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:24,580
I feel like I'm binge-watching a show every day.

119
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,880
I want to know every detail.

120
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:30,280
But it's so hard to keep it a secret.

121
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:31,760
I can't tell anyone else.

122
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:32,919
What do you think I should do?

123
00:08:32,919 --> 00:08:34,320
Thank goodness you can listen to me.

124
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:35,760
I feel much better now.

125
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:41,450
Do you feel better after talking about it?

126
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:43,480
Well...

127
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:47,560
It's just so-so.

128
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:48,960
To be honest,

129
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:51,480
it's like I'm used to drinking regular Coke,

130
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:53,480
and you suddenly give me a diet Coke.

131
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:54,960
It satisfies the craving.

132
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:56,320
But,

133
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,760
something just feels missing.

134
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,020
How far have you guys gone?

135
00:09:10,560 --> 00:09:11,920
What do you mean how far?

136
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:14,650
All I can think about lately is rehearsal.

137
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:15,730
Have you guys...

138
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:17,960
you know?

139
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:23,320
No way.

140
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:26,560
I haven't dated in years.

141
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:28,580
It can't happen that fast.

142
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:29,480
Ning Jin.

143
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:33,920
If you want your relationship to last,

144
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:37,280
intimate contact like this is essential.

145
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:38,720
Come on.

146
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,480
Remember to tell me when you get to that stage.

147
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:41,040
I swear.

148
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:43,740
I will never tell anyone else.

149
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:45,680
If I really can't hold it in,

150
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:46,340
I'll just go

151
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:47,640
talk to Jinzi.

152
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:50,800
Jinzi!

153
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:59,610
I went to the black box to get something recently.

154
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,160
The security guard at the door told me

155
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:03,090
there were strange noises inside.

156
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:05,240
He didn't know where they came from.

157
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,440
What kind of noises?

158
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,120
Rustling sounds,

159
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:09,680
from men and women.

160
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,680
It didn't sound like humans,

161
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:12,340
but ghosts.

162
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,320
Don't be afraid.

163
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:14,880
I'm here.

164
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:16,560
Baby,

165
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:18,290
let's go together tonight.

166
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:19,960
I'm not going.

167
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:21,140
Are you scared?

168
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:22,760
I'm not scared.

169
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:25,320
I just don't believe in this.

170
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,500
Then do you believe

171
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:27,660
that this ghost

172
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:29,700
is right behind everyone?

173
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:36,080
What ghosts?

174
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:37,580
Hurry up and rehearse.

175
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:40,240
Let's go.

176
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,240
Try scaring me again,

177
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:42,160
and I'll beat you to death.

178
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:44,490
Hurry up and rehearse. I'm talking to you.

179
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:45,960
Bye, director.

180
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,400
Bye.

181
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:47,960
Push harder.

182
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:48,600
Qingsong.

183
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:50,680
Push a bit harder, Qingsong.

184
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:51,880
Am I making progress?

185
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:53,720
Xixi,

186
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:54,930
you're here.

187
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:58,400
Mr. Qingsong,

188
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:00,120
I'd like to ask for your advice.

189
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:00,600
Coming.

190
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:13,800
You can go back first today.

191
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:14,720
I'm going to

192
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:18,140
have the director guide my performance privately.

193
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,840
Bro, did I do something wrong?

194
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,880
Sister Hu told me to follow you all the time.

195
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:23,280
No.

196
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,280
I saw you were working too hard,

197
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:26,960
so I asked Jinxi to give you a day off.

198
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:29,080
Tonight I'll take him to practice

199
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:29,880
the blocking privately.

200
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,120
I'm not working too hard.

201
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,680
Taking care of you is my job.

202
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:34,160
When you get tired from practicing,

203
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,890
I can buy food and water for you.

204
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,360
I'll just stay on the side.

205
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:39,020
I promise I won't disturb you.

206
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:43,920
I've been so scared these past two days.

207
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:45,080
A rat got into my house.

208
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,160
Can you help me catch it?

209
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,320
It's this big!

210
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:48,720
A rat got into your house.

211
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:50,440
It's this big!

212
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,320
It's this big!

213
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:54,970
I have a task for you.

214
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:57,360
Go to Bai Feixin's house and help her catch the rat.

215
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:58,920
How can you watch a single woman

216
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,440
stay in the same room with a rat?

217
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:01,280
Yeah.

218
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:02,280
On...

219
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:03,640
You can just find a professional online

220
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,320
to deal with it.

221
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,880
But I don't like strangers in my house.

222
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:11,960
I'm so scared.

223
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:12,240
How big?

224
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:12,760
Right.

225
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:13,080
This big!

226
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,040
How can you let her share a room with a stranger

227
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,120
or a rat?

228
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:16,720
It really is this big.

229
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:17,440
Go, Eason.

230
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:17,640
Bro.

231
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:18,760
Bye.

232
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:33,560
Why did you bring me to the theater so late?

233
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,360
To catch ghosts.

234
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:40,380
Isn't it exciting?

235
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,200
Stop joking.

236
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:43,720
Be serious.

237
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:45,420
Why are we really here?

238
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:46,690
Wait for me a moment.

239
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:05,280
I've always had a small wish,

240
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:06,120
which is

241
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:08,280
to watch a movie with my girlfriend.

242
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:12,360
But it's too much trouble for us to watch a movie alone,

243
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:13,280
so

244
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:14,960
I prepared this.

245
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:22,560
Can you help me fulfill this wish?

246
00:13:40,040 --> 00:13:40,880
Popcorn.

247
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:45,360
So what are we going to watch?

248
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,760
"The Greatest Showman"?

249
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:01,160
Because you said

250
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:03,560
your favorite movie is "The Greatest Showman".

251
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:04,800
But your biggest regret

252
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:06,120
is that you didn't go to the cinema

253
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,450
to watch it completely.

254
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:10,040
So,

255
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:13,000
do you like it?

256
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:16,880
I love it.

257
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:43,330
Who is it?

258
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:44,290
I don't know.

259
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:51,680
Why are the lights on?

260
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:56,440
Who turned on the lights?

261
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:01,680
Lao Wu.

262
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:05,440
Did you prepare all this?

263
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:17,040
I used to think

264
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:19,720
that you only brought me here to cuddle.

265
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:21,560
I didn't expect you to be so romantic today.

266
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:23,920
It's the least I could do.

267
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:29,880
Why is the popcorn open?

268
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,600
So it's easier for you to eat.

269
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:33,600
So thoughtful.

270
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:37,220
Delicious.

271
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,480
I got that for you.

272
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:46,840
What are we watching?

273
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:50,280
Guess.

274
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:52,010
You'll know when you turn it on.

275
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:56,180
The Greatest Showman.

276
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:56,960
How did you know

277
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,360
that I like this musical?

278
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:01,780
I prepared it just for you.

279
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:03,680
The mood is just right.

280
00:16:07,880 --> 00:16:08,880
I'm scared.

281
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:09,960
I'm not going.

282
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:10,240
I...

283
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,160
Over here.

284
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:12,840
Hurry.

285
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:25,680
Hurry up.

286
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:28,080
Baby.

287
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:29,320
I'm really a little scared.

288
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,480
Could there be ghosts here?

289
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:31,640
It's okay.

290
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:32,960
How could there be ghosts?

